A useful browser agent should know when not to click.

I built the handlit Agent Architect as a Chrome side-panel research agent for chat-agent design.

## Research comes before action

Give it a business website. It reads the public pages, checks the current contact paths, gathers brand language and maps the missing customer journeys.

Research stays read-mostly. Each site needs permission.

## The output is a build brief

The report includes the recommended agent role, knowledge-base outline, customer intents, sample dialogues, hand-off rules, integrations, KPIs and a system prompt.

Someone else is able to inspect the blueprint before deployment.

## Sensitive actions remain gated

Sending, buying, deleting, publishing and signing in require confirmation.

A step cap, stop control and live transcript remain visible during the run.

## The model stays replaceable

The extension is BYOK. It runs against Ollama, OpenRouter or another OpenAI-compatible endpoint.

The operator selects the model and owns the access path. The repeatable research method stays in the workflow.

Built by handlit.
